# D.Ai VM (docs/VM.md §13): a USB device given to a Windows machine is opened by QEMU as the person, in their
# own session (qemu:///session, no root). The device node must therefore be theirs: the "uaccess" tag gives the
# user at the seat an ACL on it while they are logged in, and takes it away when they log out (systemd-logind).
# Hubs (device class 09) are left alone. This is the same mechanism distributions use for cameras and
# scanners; it means any program of the logged-in user may talk to a plugged-in USB device directly
# (the person's own devices, in their own session). Requires a check on real hardware before release.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{bDeviceClass}!="09", TAG+="uaccess"
